Description: Age, sex and race matched United States reference survival, as
    consumed by clinical outcomes reports within The Heart and Vascular
    Institute at the Cleveland Clinic. Reproduces the 'SAS' macro
    'usmatchd', which evaluates a stored three-phase parametric hazard fit
    of Blackstone, Naftel and Turner (1986)
    <doi:10.1080/01621459.1986.10478314> on the age axis rather than
    interpolating a life table. Ships the fitted parameter blocks, one set
    per vintage per stratum, together with a thin evaluator over the
    'TemporalHazard' package. The reference vintage is never defaulted, so
    an analysis must state which reference population it used.
